{"id":"cd9589bb0f042208","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability.md","title":"Arithmetic Hierarchy Stability","display":"thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability — Arithmetic Hierarchy Stability","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability","aliases":["58-thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability"],"display":"thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability — Arithmetic Hierarchy Stability","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability — Arithmetic Hierarchy Stability"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1d779f4a08a1f22e\" href=\"?note=1d779f4a08a1f22e\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md\">../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\\in V\">\\(\\Sigma\\in V\\)</span> is an arithmetic signature and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Delta_n^0(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Delta_n^0(\\Sigma)\\)</span> are the formula classes from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1d779f4a08a1f22e\" href=\"?note=1d779f4a08a1f22e\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md\">../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-delta}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\n\\Delta_n^0(\\Sigma)=\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma)\\cap\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma)\n\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-delta}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\n\\Delta_n^0(\\Sigma)=\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma)\\cap\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma)\n\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-zero}\\vdash\n\\Sigma_0^0(\\Sigma)=\\Pi_0^0(\\Sigma)=\\Delta_0^0(\\Sigma)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-zero}\\vdash\n\\Sigma_0^0(\\Sigma)=\\Pi_0^0(\\Sigma)=\\Delta_0^0(\\Sigma)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-cross}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\n\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\Sigma_{n+1}^0(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\Pi_{n+1}^0(\\Sigma)\n\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-cross}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\n\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\Sigma_{n+1}^0(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\Pi_{n+1}^0(\\Sigma)\n\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>These are facts about the syntactic formula classes defined upstream. The cross-inclusions use the permitted empty quantifier block.</li>\n<li>Strict separation of the semantic pointclasses requires an arithmetic coding, truth/realization semantics, and a diagonal argument; it is not asserted from the bare syntactic recursion alone.</li>\n<li>Sets and relations inherit a complexity level only through a separate definition of what it means for a formula to define them.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md","status":"resolved","id":"1d779f4a08a1f22e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md","status":"resolved","id":"1d779f4a08a1f22e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Delta_n^0(\\Sigma)$ are the formula classes from [[../batch17/58-df-arithmetic-hierarchy.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma),\\Delta_n^0(\\Sigma)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-delta}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\n\\Delta_n^0(\\Sigma)=\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma)\\cap\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma)\n\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-zero}\\vdash\n\\Sigma_0^0(\\Sigma)=\\Pi_0^0(\\Sigma)=\\Delta_0^0(\\Sigma)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}arithmetic-hierarchy-stability-cross}\\vdash\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\n\\Pi_n^0(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\Sigma_{n+1}^0(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\Sigma_n^0(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\Pi_{n+1}^0(\\Sigma)\n\\bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1575,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4029","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability.md|58-thm-arithmetic-hierarchy-stability]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["1d779f4a08a1f22e"]}